<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brazilian Historical and Geographic Institute</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1838</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Instituto Histórico e Geográfico Brasileiro, Brazilian Historical and Geographical Institute</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Brazilian Historical and Geographic Institute is a learned society founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a> in 1838 to collect documents and write a national history of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>. Closely patronised by Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-ii-of-brazil">Pedro II</a>, who attended hundreds of its sessions, it shaped the official image of the empire's past and published a long-running journal. It still exists and is the oldest institution of its kind in Brazil.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brazilian-historical-and-geographic-institute.jpg" alt="Brazilian Historical and Geographic Institute" width="320" height="156" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Instituto Histórico e Geográfico Brasileiro · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblema_do_Instituto_Hist%C3%B3rico_e_Geogr%C3%A1fico_Brasileiro.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
